1
00:00:03,099 --> 00:00:06,090
Lesson 19, Nicole's close election.

2
00:00:06,940 --> 00:00:09,370
Nicole loses the election at school.

3
00:00:10,039 --> 00:00:13,570
She doesn't want to accept it so she looks for excuses.

4
00:00:14,560 --> 00:00:18,089
Ted encourages her to accept defeat and move on.

5
00:00:19,059 --> 00:00:24,410
I lost the election by a hair, just ten votes, but I'm not giving up.

6
00:00:24,719 --> 00:00:25,729
Give me a break, Nicole.

7
00:00:26,059 --> 00:00:26,549
You lost.

8
00:00:26,839 --> 00:00:27,469
Live with it.

9
00:00:27,780 --> 00:00:29,129
But I was a sure thing.

10
00:00:28,980 --> 00:00:33,909
If I hadn't stayed up so late baking cookies, I wouldn't have messed up my speech.

11
00:00:34,020 --> 00:00:35,089
Get real, Nicole.

12
00:00:35,640 --> 00:00:36,850
It's your fault, Ted.

13
00:00:37,240 --> 00:00:39,670
I lost because your friends didn't vote for me.

14
00:00:40,020 --> 00:00:41,530
Don't try to put the blame on me.

15
00:00:42,020 --> 00:00:43,129
I gave it my best shot.

16
00:00:43,700 --> 00:00:46,070
They must have made a mistake while counting the votes.

17
00:00:46,460 --> 00:00:49,369
I'll demand a recount on Monday and set the record straight.

18
00:00:49,760 --> 00:00:51,549
Don't make a fool of yourself, Nicole.

19
00:00:51,979 --> 00:00:52,549
Face it.

20
00:00:52,840 --> 00:00:54,829
Andrea won the election fair and square.

21
00:00:55,310 --> 00:00:57,949
Well, I just don't know where I went wrong.

22
00:00:58,920 --> 00:01:01,170
Here, take a chocolate chip cookie.

23
00:01:01,560 --> 00:01:03,250
That'll cheer you up for sure.

